IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-proc-director-interests`

-- Tests for sg-proc-director-interests.l4 (s 156 and s 162 of the Companies Act 1967: the procedure for a declaration of interest and for a restricted transaction).
-- Every expected outcome below was written from the text (src:12938-13168 and src:13411-13566 of CoA1967.txt) before the module was run,
-- never copied from its output. A trace that does not match is a finding. Day 0 of each trace is the day the TIMELINE line above its rule names.

§ `Helpers: s 162(3), (4) and (10)`

-- Arguments of (3)(a) or (b): the expenditure; the home; another home transaction outstanding.
#ASSERT `s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(3)(a) or (b) the transaction is within one of the two paragraphs` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- Prior approval: approved at a general meeting with the disclosures; the day approved; the day the transaction was made. Approval after the transaction does not count (s 162(10)).
#ASSERT `s 162(4)(a) the company gave prior approval as the paragraph requires` TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s 162(4)(a) the company gave prior approval as the paragraph requires` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(4)(a) the company gave prior approval as the paragraph requires` TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(4)(a) the company gave prior approval as the paragraph requires` FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026))

-- Approved at or before the next following annual general meeting, which concludes on 30 April 2026: approved; the day approved; the day the transaction was made (1 February 2026); the day that meeting concludes. An approval after the transaction does not count (s 162(10)).
#ASSERT `s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT `s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` TRUE (Date 1 5 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(4)(b) the approval was given at or before the next following annual general meeting` FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026))

-- The days from 1 February 2026 to 30 October 2026 (30 April 2026 plus 6 months): 28+31+30+31+30+31+31+30 = 242 to 1 October, and 29 more.
#ASSERT `s 162(4)(b) the days from the day of the transaction to the last day for repayment or discharge` (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 30 4 2026) EQUALS 271

-- Arguments: the expenditure; the home; another home transaction outstanding; approved; the day approved; the day made; the condition of (4)(b).
#ASSERT `s 162(3) and (4) the transaction is within paragraph (a) or (b) and subsection (4) authorises it` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 162(3) and (4) the transaction is within paragraph (a) or (b) and subsection (4) authorises it` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(3) and (4) the transaction is within paragraph (a) or (b) and subsection (4) authorises it` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 162(3) and (4) the transaction is within paragraph (a) or (b) and subsection (4) authorises it` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE)

§ `s 156(1), (9), (10) and (11): the declaration, the copy and the minutes`

-- Arguments: the declarant; the company; the secretary; a director or chief executive officer; interested; not deemed interested by subsection (4); only a member or creditor of a corporation; not a material interest.
-- A declaration at a meeting on day 3, and the secretary minutes it on day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(1)(a) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors of the company` AT 3
    PARTY Secretary "S" DOES `s 156(11) record the declaration in the minutes of the meeting at which it was made` AT 3

-- A declaration at a meeting on day 3 and no minute yet: the secretary's duty is open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(1)(a) declare the nature of the interest at a meeting of the directors of the company` AT 3

-- A written notice on day 5, the company's copy on day 6, the minute of the next meeting on day 12.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(1)(b) send a written notice to the company on the nature, character and extent of the interest` AT 5
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 156(9) send a copy of the written notice to all the directors, or all the other directors where a director gave it` AT 6
    PARTY Secretary "S" DOES `s 156(10)(b) record the declaration in the minutes of the next meeting of the directors after the notice is given, as if it had been made at that meeting` AT 12

-- A written notice and the copy, and no minute yet: the secretary's duty is open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(1)(b) send a written notice to the company on the nature, character and extent of the interest` AT 5
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 156(9) send a copy of the written notice to all the directors, or all the other directors where a director gave it` AT 6

-- Nothing done after 400 days: "as soon as is practicable" is no number, so nothing lapses and nothing is breached.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- The interest is only that of a member of a corporation that is interested, and not material (s 156(3)): nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- The person is not deemed interested by reason only of a guarantee or an office (s 156(4)): nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(1) the director or chief executive officer must declare the interest or send a written notice, and the company and the secretary follow` (Director "D") (Company "Co") (Secretary "S") TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 156(6) to (8): the conflict of duty or interest`

-- Arguments: the declarant; a director or chief executive officer; holds the office or property; already a director when he or she commenced to hold it; the day became a director (1 January 2026);
-- the day commenced to hold it (10 March 2026, day 0); the dates of the meetings of the directors (5 March, 20 March, 1 April 2026). The first meeting after day 0 is 20 March, day 10.
-- The last day: the declaration at the first meeting, day 10.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company` AT 10

-- In time: the written notice on day 3, before the first meeting.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict` AT 3

-- After the first meeting with nothing done (day 15): the declaration route has lapsed, the written notice has no day, so the duty is still open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

-- After the first meeting, the written notice on day 15 still discharges the duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 12)
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(6)(b) send a written notice to the company on the conflict` AT 15

-- A declaration at the later meeting of 1 April (day 22) is not the declaration at the first meeting, so it does not discharge the duty.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 20 3 2026), (Date 1 4 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company` AT 22

-- No meeting has been held after day 0 (the one meeting listed is before it): no first meeting, no clock, and a declaration on day 50 discharges the duty. The day-50 meeting is not in the list; the trace shows only that no clock applies.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 5 3 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(6)(a) declare the conflict at a meeting of the directors of the company` AT 50

-- The person holds no office or property in conflict: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(6) the director or chief executive officer must declare the conflict, at the first meeting if by declaration` (Director "D") TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 10 3 2026) (LIST (Date 20 3 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 156(15): the offence`

-- A director fails to comply with a provision of the section on day 40: the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 156(15) a director or chief executive officer must not fail to comply with a provision of section 156` (Director "D") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(15) fail to comply with a provision of section 156` AT 40

-- No failure: the prohibition stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 156(15) a director or chief executive officer must not fail to comply with a provision of section 156` (Director "D") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- The person is neither a director nor a chief executive officer: the offence does not reach the person.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 156(15) a director or chief executive officer must not fail to comply with a provision of section 156` (Director "D") FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 156(15) fail to comply with a provision of section 156` AT 40

§ `s 162(2): the company must not make a restricted transaction`

-- Arguments: the company; an exempt private company; within section 163A or 163B or (3)(c) or (d); the expenditure of (3)(a); the home of (3)(b); another home transaction outstanding;
-- approved at a general meeting with the disclosures; the day approved; the day the transaction was made (1 February 2026, day 0); the condition of (4)(b).
-- An exempt private company makes the transaction: the bar does not reach it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- A company that is not exempt makes a restricted transaction within no exception.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- The same company does not make it: the bar stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Expenditure for the company's purposes with prior approval given on 15 January: within (3)(a) and (4)(a).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- Approval given on the day of the transaction is not given after it (s 162(10)), so it counts.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- Approval given on 2 February, after the transaction, does not count (s 162(10)), and there is no condition: the company contravenes.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 2 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- No prior approval, but the transaction is made on the condition of (4)(b): the making is within the exception.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- The transaction is within section 163A or 163B or (3)(c) or (d): the bar does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- A home transaction while another is outstanding is outside (3)(b), even with approval before.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(2) the company must not make the restricted transaction unless it is exempt or an exception or an approval takes it outside the bar` (Company "Co") FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(2) the company makes the restricted transaction` AT 0

§ `s 162(4)(b): repayment within six months from the next annual general meeting`

-- Arguments: the company; the director who owes the amount; the expenditure of (3)(a); the home of (3)(b); another home transaction outstanding; approved at a general meeting with the disclosures; the day approved;
-- the day the transaction was made (1 February 2026, day 0); the condition of (4)(b); the day the next following annual general meeting concludes (30 April 2026). The last day for repayment is 30 October 2026, day 271.
-- The last day: repaid on day 271.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(4)(b) repay the amount of the restricted transaction or discharge the liability under it` AT 271

-- In time: repaid on day 100.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(4)(b) repay the amount of the restricted transaction or discharge the liability under it` AT 100

-- One day late: repaid on day 272.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(4)(b) repay the amount of the restricted transaction or discharge the liability under it` AT 272

-- Day 200, not yet repaid: the six months are still running.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 200)

-- Day 300, not repaid: the six months are over and the condition has failed.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 300)

-- Approval given at the annual general meeting itself (30 April) is after the transaction, so it is not prior approval (s 162(10)): the amount must still be repaid by day 271.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 300)

-- Approval given on 15 January, before the transaction, meets the condition: nothing to repay.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 300)

-- Approval given on 15 May, after the meeting and the transaction, does not count: the amount must still be repaid by day 271.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 5 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 300)

-- The transaction was not made on the condition: no repayment duty arises under (4)(b).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(4)(b) the amount must be repaid or the liability discharged within 6 months from the conclusion of the next annual general meeting` (Company "Co") (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) FALSE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 300)

§ `s 162(5): the indemnity`

-- Arguments: the authorising director; the expenditure; the home; another home transaction outstanding; approved; the day approved; the day the transaction was made (1 February 2026); the condition of (4)(b); the day the next following annual general meeting concludes (30 April 2026).
-- No approval at or before the meeting: the authorising director indemnifies the company on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction must indemnify the company against the loss` (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(5) indemnify the company against the loss arising from the restricted transaction` AT 5

-- No approval, and no indemnity yet: the duty is open, with no day.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction must indemnify the company against the loss` (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Approval was given at the meeting (30 April), after the transaction, so it does not count (s 162(10)): the indemnity is owed and not yet given.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction must indemnify the company against the loss` (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- Approval was given on 15 January, before the transaction: nothing is owed under (5).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(5) the directors who authorised the transaction must indemnify the company against the loss` (Director "D") TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 15 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) TRUE (Date 30 4 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 162(6): the offence of the authorising director`

-- The company contravened section 162 and the director authorises the making on day 0: the offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 162(6) where the company contravenes section 162 a director must not authorise the making of the restricted transaction` (Director "D") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(6) authorise the making of the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- The company did not contravene section 162: authorising the making is no offence.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(6) where the company contravenes section 162 a director must not authorise the making of the restricted transaction` (Director "D") FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D" DOES `s 162(6) authorise the making of the restricted transaction` AT 0

-- The company contravened and no director has authorised the making: the bar stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(6) where the company contravenes section 162 a director must not authorise the making of the restricted transaction` (Director "D") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

§ `s 162(7): recovery of the amount`

-- The amount is owed under a dealing contrary to section 162 and the company recovers it on day 40.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(7) the company may recover the amount of a dealing made contrary to section 162` (Company "Co") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Co" DOES `s 162(7) recover the amount of the loan, quasi-loan, credit transaction or arrangement, or the amount for which the company becomes liable` AT 40

-- The company has not yet recovered it: the liberty stays open, with no day.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 162(7) the company may recover the amount of a dealing made contrary to section 162` (Company "Co") TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- The amount is not owed under a dealing contrary to section 162: the subsection gives nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 162(7) the company may recover the amount of a dealing made contrary to section 162` (Company "Co") FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
--   None by outcome class. All 45 traces above give the same class (FULFILLED, BREACH or RESIDUAL) on the stable build (cache entry 112) as on the unstable build (20261125, a50cbd0),
--   and all 18 assertions are satisfied on both. (The layout of a still-open result was not compared.)
